From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sprd: ums512: raise the thermal passive trip to 85 C

All eleven ums512 thermal zones throttle from a 70 C passive trip, which is
far too early for this die: the critical trip sits at 110 C, and stock Android
runs its control loop at 85 C (soc-thmzone's second passive trip, the one that
carries every cooling-map; 70 C is only the governor switch-on point there).

With no sustainable-power the zones use step_wise, so crossing 70 C walks the
cooling device one state further every polling interval until it saturates. On
an RG Rotate that pins the little cluster at its lowest OPP within about three
seconds of load, with the die still nearly 40 C below critical:

  50878 mC  2002000
  65842 mC  1144000
  66616 mC   614400
  ...
  72550 mC   614400     <- 614 MHz, cooling_device8 (cpufreq-cpu0) at 9/9

614 MHz at 66 C is not usable for the workloads this SoC ships in. Adopt
stock's 85 C control temperature, and widen the hysteresis to 2 C so the
device is not re-armed by sensor noise.

Only the temperature changes. Every zone keeps its own passive trip and
cooling-map on purpose: the per-core sensors (ank0..ank5, prometheus6,
prometheus7) run considerably hotter than the cluster-top ones under sustained
load, and the thermal core takes the highest cooling state any zone asks for,
so leaving them all armed lets whichever core is actually hottest drive the
throttling. Reducing this to one controller per cooling device on the
cluster-top sensors was tried and is wrong - cputop1 was still below 85 C while
prometheus7 reached its 110 C critical trip and shut the board down.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512.dtsi
@@ -2305,8 +2305,8 @@
 
 				trips {
 					cputop0_alert0: trip-point0 {
-						temperature = <70000>;
-						hysteresis = <1000>;
+						temperature = <85000>;
+						hysteresis = <2000>;
 						type = "passive";
 					};
 
